      <description>&lt;div class="wi_fic_desc" property="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;The city of New Caldera's walls were supposed to be impenetrable, able to keep the apocalyptic danger of the Shattered Lands outside while sealing the residents inside. But no seal can ever last forever. A weakpoint forms, which lengthens into a tear. A tear that someone could escape through. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Lady Eleanor is a woman who, for all intents and purposes, doesn't exist. She feels trapped. Trapped by the society of Caldera in which she is forced to live. Trapped by her father and his terrible expectations. Trapped by the very body she resides in. Trapped until she discovers it. Proof that her cage is not impenetrable. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;She must navigate the Shattered Lands, meeting friendly faces, fighting terrible foes, and discovering who she desperately wants to be along the way. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
