    <item>
      <title>Borrowed</title>
      <author> BrynnChappell </author>
      <link>https://www.scribblehub.com/series/2697159/borrowed/</link>
      <comments>https://www.scribblehub.com/read/2697159-borrowed/chapter/2697169/#comments</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">637f0c9ac39698c6a08cad67a72a0fed87eaf510</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div class="wi_fic_desc" property="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;"You don't get my flip. You don't get me. Figure out who you are."&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;This illustrated romance novel includes nineteen full-color illustrations inside.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Carver State cut men's diving in August. By October, I was teaching cheerleaders to twist for fourteen bucks an hour until their star flyer blew out her knee right before the qualifier.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;A missing flyer meant a lost bid. Twenty girls would forfeit their scholarships. I was the only person left on campus who had the exact skills needed to fly her spot and save the program. I threw on a copper wig. I wore a borrowed number. A case of fake laryngitis kept my voice disguised while we practiced our intense routine on the mat. The plan was incredibly simple. I would hit the routine and give the uniform back. But the plan didn't account for Sol Reyes, the strict captain who spots every move I make from the bottom of the stunt and refuses to fall for her flyer again. It didn't account for Avery Vance. The rival captain keeps looking at my jersey. And it definitely didn't account for the girl in the mirror, who smiles wider and appears happier than I ever have before.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Everyone keeps saying this uniform is just a costume. They tell me to take it off. But it fits perfectly, and it provides more comfort than any other clothing I've ever worn in my entire life.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Borrowed is a grounded gender transition romance. The story features a college diver finding out who she has been all along through an honest and realistic journey based on the author's own experiences with gender transition, without any forced feminization tropes.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;It spans roughly one hundred thousand words. Rowan and Sol share alternating chapters. This closed-door sports romance explores a questioning trans heroine engaging in a forbidden relationship while crossing paths with a new chosen family.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;She crossdresses to save the team. Both athletes navigate their secret identities.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Based on the author's own gender transition, this book is one hundred percent human. Zero artificial intelligence touched these pages. Every single word was crafted by a human author typing on a keyboard, and absolutely no generative AI tools were used to write or illustrate this novel.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
