      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div class="wi_fic_desc" property="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;A new VRMMO called LightStorm has just released, boasting immersive Full Dive support, a huge dynamic world, and accurate (non-sentient) personality constructs for every single NPC. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Kathy, a student at a small Australian university, has been waiting for this game since she was a tween.&lt;br /&gt; She comes to find that while the NPC's are immersive and have tons of depth, they are restricted in terms of romance to at least attempt to keep the game's rating down. Flirting with them is like trying to seduce a brick wall, and she's a little disappointed. Flirting with NPCs wasn't the whole reason she wanted to play of course, but it was at least a factor! Social anxiety always screwed her over, especially around pretty girls, and being able to practice on some low-stakes non-feeling AI would have been nice. &lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;She then meets Mari, an NPC who recently graduated from the prestigious Grand Carneth Academy and ran away from home. Mari has found herself in a hard spot, and Kathy is given a System Quest (very rare!) to help her out.&lt;br /&gt; Mari should just be another surface level NPC, but she is utterly gorgeous and Kathy ends up flirting with her anyway. What's the worst that could happen? Surely the flush on Mari's cute cheeks doesn't mean anything significant...&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;----&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;A personal project I'm using to practice my writing! I cannot promise consistent chapters, audhd is fickle and mean and the medication even more so, but I will try my best! Positive comments greatly boost my motivation so if you want more chapters please tell me!&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;No AI was used except for basic proofreading (with a local model running on my pc, so no data centres) mostly just because I have no beta readers and don't trust my own eyes. If anyone would like to beta feel free to throw me a message!&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
