      <description>&lt;div class="wi_fic_desc" property="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Haruki Shinohara is sixteen. He's small. He's soft. He's bullied for looking like a girl. His three older brothers are everything he's not—tall, handsome, and cruel. His parents treat him like a disappointment. He eats lunch alone in a hallway. He has given up.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Then a transfer student walks in wearing a skirt.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Kanade Hoshikawa doesn't care what anyone thinks. He wears makeup. He paints his nails. He hands Haruki a tube of lip gloss on a rooftop and kisses him before he can say no.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;That kiss changes everything.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;What starts as a simple BL romance between two feminine boys slowly becomes something else. Something bigger. A story about two people discovering who they really are. About three brothers who failed their sibling and spent years trying to make it right. About a family that wasn't born—it was built. From lip gloss. From wagyu beef. From a house with no walls. From a laminated set of rules on a fridge.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;This is not a story about becoming a woman. This is a story about becoming a person. And the people who hold your hand while you do.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
